From 223553bb814e25d1296bd4a92379b0f479934f0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Paprocki <hi@rpaprocki.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:44:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/26] pull model: dispatch the encrypted config as a workflow
 input

Upstream wrote the config to temp_zips/, gave GitHub a URL pointing back
at this server (built from the request's Host header) and made the runner
download it from /get_zip, plus the images from /get_png. So rdgen had to
be reachable from the internet. This commit keeps everything outbound:

  inputs = {version, cfg, build_uuid, proto}
  cfg    = base64(AES-256 zip(secrets.json + assets/{icon,logo,privacy}.png))

- rdgenerator/buildcfg.py: images (upload or data: URI) are decoded with a
  pixel cap, re-encoded (which strips metadata and trailing data) and
  shrunk step by step (palette quantization, then smaller sides) until
  the dispatch payload fits GitHub's 65,535-character input limit, using
  a 65,000 budget. If it still does not fit, the build is refused with a
  clear 413 message instead of silently dropping the images.
- The zip is built in memory. Nothing is written to temp_zips/ or png/
  any more.
- secrets.json only carries the icon/logo/privacy flags
  ('embedded'/'false'), not callback URLs. genurl is gone.
- rdgenerator/github.py: small REST client. The token is only ever in the
  Authorization header. Owner/repo are validated before they go into
  URL paths (upstream concatenated them). Errors are sanitized (status
  plus GitHub's message, never headers). return_run_details:true gives
  the run id; a 204 from an older API is tolerated (the poller then finds
  the run by its run-name).
- proto=1 is sent with every dispatch. The workflows require the same
  value, and GitHub answers 422 for undeclared inputs, so a server and a
  build repository that are out of sync fail at dispatch, not halfway
  through a build.
- Removed the SH_SECRET "self-hosted" branch and GENURL/PROTOCOL.
- Optional site defaults (RDGEN_DEFAULT_SERVER/_API_SERVER/_KEY or
  _KEY_FILE, e.g. the hbbs id_ed25519.pub in the same LXC) prefill the
  form. A blank server/key/API field in an API call uses them instead of
  RustDesk's public servers.
- Model: AutoField PK (upstream's IntegerField PK never learned the rowid,
  so a second save() inserted a duplicate), unique uuid, platform,
  filename, version, timestamps, file manifest, fetched artifact ids,
  last_error, poll_failures (migration 0003).
- Dispatch failures are shown on the form or returned as JSON (502/503)
  instead of a bare JsonResponse page. Oversized API bodies get 413 JSON.

